ng other  others wearing masks is a source of  great reassurance and people want to do  it  okay uh the old trafford question  manchester united playing leads 14th of  august  um are you fine with 74 000 people  turning up  most of them without masks well as  sirian said i don't think we know that  it's most of them without masks and i do  know having a long-standing relationship  with manchester united they're in my  constituency here  um that they will go to great lengths to  to keep people safe  and make sure that protections and  mitigations are in place  are you you're going to be there right  no i'm not sadly i'm this ticket you're  offering if it's still going spare you  know send it my way but um  i would really encourage people who are  going to that game to keep themselves  and others around them safe and please  wear a mask and follow the instructions  that stewards are giving you  um because you know it's it's outdoors  there's less risk of infection spreading  when you are outdoors as  as we know but i think every measure  that we can take we should take  uh to defeat this terrible virus okay  you you've issued a statement today  about the government's plans for  legislation against hate speech  in higher education and  what you said or what the party has said  in its  release is labor say the law is trying  to solve the problem doesn't exist  uh let me read you some names jk rowling  julie bindle amber rudd selena todd  kevin price uh you know what they've all  got in common they have all been  cancelled in fact one of them's lost  their job over the what they have said  about the issue of women as a sex  uh as opposed to um the the view that's  taken by some  trans rights activists that uh there is  no such thing essentially  now are you really saying that there is  nothing to see here this problem doesn't  exist  there are and always have been a small  a very small number of instances and  i think those uh examples that you gave  um in many cases perhaps in all cases  i'm not familiar with every single one  of those examples trevor  uh well please but trevor  last in the last year for which we have  data out of 10 000 events  only six were cancelled four because  they had the wrong paperwork  one went to another venue one was a  pyramid scheme if you look across the  piece  there are a very small number of events  that are cancelled i think there is  obviously a concern about the atmosphere  the climate on campus  but that cuts both ways and if we have  as i believe this legislation does  um a law that allows people actually to  come on campus as  holocaust deniers to spread hate speech  anti-faxers  i don't think that's in the public  interest and i think that has a chilling  effect and i think  we don't need this legislation we  already have faithful  on campus in law and i think that this  actually  gives sucker to people who want to sow  hate and division  and to their lawyers they'll be running  off particularly  on the basis of a small number of cases  if i may say so you say it's a small  number of cases  but for every individual who is fired  because of what they have said  it's a hundred percent so let me just  ask you again  is the labor view it that nothing to see  here  i'm not saying there are no cases at all  what i am saying is  it's a very small number of incidents  when you look at the number of events  that have gone ahead  quite satisfactorily on campus and that  we already have  satisfactory legislation we've had it  going back to the 1986 education act  and then strengthened i would say by  labour's human rights act  what we don't need is legislation that  now allows holocaust deniers  anti-vaxxers people spreading hate  speech  to run off to the courts if a student  union or university says  okay all right um i don't want that and  i don't think  okay kate green i know you know a lot  about education but i think you know  quite a lot about football as well  what's a score tonight  what is 